diff --git a/docs/sequoia-v121.md b/docs/sequoia-v121.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..09919f0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/sequoia-v121.md
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# TOTK 1.2.1 on macOS Sequoia
+
+This checkout combines the community `m3-macos15` branch at
+`f71ea7b56eb1f7064d5e753428cc6b05a124241b` with the upstream 1.2.1 support from
+`2db612bd7a82db2d94e3929556b71f0200f4b08c`.
+
+The 1.2.1 ExeFS and rewritten module hashes are upstream's published hashes.
+Version offsets, runtime tables, RomFS overlays and the launcher select `v121`.
+The added `runtime-v121-m3` target uses the community Metal 3 graphics backend and
+targets macOS 15.0. Build with `TOTK_M3=1`, the 1.0.0 base and a separate 1.2.1
+update.
+
+Updated builds use the update's complete ExeFS and validate its NPDM. The base
+provides RomFS; its executable module hashes and the base and merged RomFS hashes
+are still checked. The unused base NPDM can differ between NSP and cartridge
+sources and is not loaded by an updated build.
+
+`assets/shared-fonts-22.1.0.json` adds one complete, pinned firmware font set.
+The source data NCAs passed their FS-header and six-level IVFC checks; every
+decoded font passed all sfnt table checksums and the whole-font checksum. The
+original font set remains supported. Mixed sets and unknown bytes are rejected;
+the runtime also checks each bundled font's hash.
+
+Build intermediates and the output App must be outside this source checkout.
+The build requires Python 3.14, Xcode command line tools, and Homebrew `opus` and
+`libvpx`. No game data, font data or keys belong in this source checkout.
+
+After signing and verifying the freshly built local App, the packager removes
+an inherited quarantine attribute from that bundle before its first launch.
+This fixes the build host's `0081;00000000;;` marker rejecting an otherwise
+valid local ad-hoc signature.
